    Bug 1915259 - Fix inconsistent value (null vs. undefind) in MailFolder.subFolders. r=aleca

    This fixes a bug, but will change extension behavior (this is why a
    test has to be changed).

    A `MailFolder` returned as the `rootFolder` of an account will have its
    `subFolders` property be `null`, if subfolders are not requested. All
    functions from the folders API return `undefined` in this case.

    The `rootFolder` property which is changed was only introduced recently
    in Thunderbird 121 (Bug 1863269). I evaluated the chance to permanently
    break add-ons to be very low, because the feature can only be used by
    add-ons which have been updated recently and therefore have an active
    maintainer. I will monitor extensions and help developers to mitigate
    the change.

    Extensions are affected, if they explicitly check for

    `rootFolder.subFolders === null`

    I did not find affected add-ons on ATN.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220337

diff --git a/mail/components/extensions/ExtensionAccounts.sys.mjs b/mail/components/extensions/ExtensionAccounts.sys.mjs
index 0e5f64353e8..99f608e32d7 100644
--- a/mail/components/extensions/ExtensionAccounts.sys.mjs
+++ b/mail/components/extensions/ExtensionAccounts.sys.mjs
@@ -98,12 +98,12 @@ export class AccountManager {
         account.key
       );
       mailAccount.rootFolder.subFolders = subFolders;
-    } else if (this.extension.manifestVersion < 3) {
-      mailAccount.rootFolder.subFolders = null;
     }

     if (this.extension.manifestVersion < 3) {
-      mailAccount.folders = mailAccount.rootFolder.subFolders;
+      mailAccount.folders = includeFolders
+        ? mailAccount.rootFolder.subFolders
+        : null;
     }

     return mailAccount;
